### Import checklist

1. Choose padded PNGs OR atlas slices. Registration and padding are already baked. Do not add the recorded translation again.
2. Apply density compensation once. Do not combine PPU with another compensating transform, body_scale_ratio or density_factor_to_ready. Sweep ready/action textures intentionally have different densities.
3. Convert top-left pixel pivot to normalized bottom-left using (x/width, 1−y/height). Already-normalized Unity pivots need no second Y flip. Run slice sizes vary slightly; use the companion’s exact conversions.
4. Preserve authored body bob and cell-relative motion. Do not stack another silhouette-centering, per-frame fit, stabilization or root-movement pass on top of existing registration.
5. Keep the native sources and delivered runtime pixels unchanged. No mirrored substitutes or new upscaling. Sweep DR is an explicit exception to untouched native runtime: its high-resolution masters were Lanczos-resampled as whole images. Other sweep headings use native pixels with baked integer placements.
6. Review ready ↔ action joins at gameplay size. Feet, props and endpoints may shift. UL actions can expose a trailing far sword that shared ready hides forward. No seamless transition or physical foot-contact claim is made.

